src(11,'CBI v. V. C. Shukla and others','Supreme Court of India; Indian Kanoon reproduction','https://indiankanoon.org/doc/320053/','1998-03-02','Court record','Final evidentiary analysis and disposition, lines271–299','Court found no prima facie case against Advani and Shukla on the material presented and dismissed CBI appeals. Entries alone did not establish the alleged payments; admissions by the Jains could not be used as admissions by Advani.','Charge-stage evidentiary disposition; not a conviction or a trial acquittal. The court left the then public-servant question open.',origin='SC-CBI-SHUKLA-1998')
src(12,'Babri demolition: 32 accused acquitted','Asad Rehman, Indian Express','https://indianexpress.com/article/india/babri-masjid-ayodhya-demolition-verdict-advani-mm-joshi-uma-bharti-accused-acquitted-6645770/lite/','2020-09-30','Journalism','Verdict and reactions, lines48–49,95–121','Special CBI court acquitted all32 accused including Advani for lack of conclusive evidence. Prosecution alleged conspiracy and instigation; accused denied wrongdoing and alleged political implication. Advani welcomed the decision as vindication of commitment to the temple movement.','Trial judgment not inspected in full. Separately reports 2017 restoration of conspiracy charges. Do not conflate criminal outcome with inquiry findings or title litigation.',origin='CBI-TRIAL-2020-report-IE')
src(13,'HC dismisses appeal against Babri acquittal','Indian Express','https://indianexpress.com/article/cities/lucknow/babri-masjid-demolition-case-hc-dismisses-plea-against-acquittal-of-advani-others-8259632/','2022-11-10','Journalism','Order reported9 November; lines20–35','Allahabad High Court dismissed the two appellants’ challenge because they lacked standing as victims under the applicable appeal provision; the appeal was against the30 September2020 acquittal.','Standing decision, not a fresh merits adjudication. Latest procedural report inspected; no claim that all possible later litigation has been exhaustively excluded.',origin='ALLHC-2022-11-09')
src(14,'Liberhan report: levels of culpability','NDTV Correspondent','https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/liberhan-report-levels-of-culpability-405456','2009-11-24','Commission reproduction','Report summary lines225–248; list item29','Commission attributed responsibility to senior BJP/RSS leadership and included Advani among68 persons considered culpable; distinguished leaders’ political and ideological responsibility from different operational roles.','Secondary selection from inquiry report, not criminal conviction. Full original findings and precise paragraph boundaries remain a gap.',origin='LIBERHAN-2009')
src(15,'Annual Report 2003–2004','Ministry of Home Affairs','https://www.mha.gov.in/sites/default/files/ar0304-Eng_4.pdf','2004','Official record','Paras1.21–1.30;3.34–3.40; AnnexureI','Lists Advani as Deputy PM and Home Minister at31 March2004. National identity-card pilot began April2003 in13 states/UTs; citizenship registration rules notified10 December2003. Citizenship amendment notified8 January2004. Police modernisation plan approved February2002; ministry reports expenditure. Advani met Ansari-led Hurriyat22 January and27 March2004; detention reviews recommended43 releases by31 March. Disaster-preparedness work and a proposed national authority are described.','Ministry self-report. Distinguish pilot, expenditure, recommendation and completed outcome. Overseas citizenship is not full dual citizenship or voting rights; proposed authority is not an established statutory NDMA.')
src(16,'Joint sitting: Prevention of Terrorism Bill','Parliament of India; Indian Kanoon reproduction','https://indiankanoon.org/doc/588563/','2002-03-26','Parliamentary record','Advani introduction; ruling on joint sitting; opposition speeches; concluding vote','Advani moved POTA and argued special law was needed against terrorism; linked the proposal to Parliament attack and post-9/11 international measures. Opposition challenged safeguards, selective use and the procedure. Chair ruled Rajya Sabha rejection enabled Article108 joint sitting.','Speech claims and accusations remain attributed. The debate does not establish that POTA reduced terrorism.',origin='PARLIAMENT-POTA-2002-03-26')
src(17,'Broadcasting autonomy and Prasar Bharati','Yojana, Publications Division','https://www.publicationsdivision.nic.in/journals/Journalarchives/Yojana/Yojana-English/1997/October/Yojana_1997_October_2062495762.pdf','1997-10','Official record','PDF p.6; broadcasting-autonomy historical discussion','Verghese group proposed a national broadcasting trust. The1979 Prasar Bharati bill retained greater government direction powers than the recommendations; protested in Parliament, it died with the Janata government. A new bill followed under the National Front in1989.','Government journal retrospective; source supports the legislative distinction, not an outcome measure of media independence.')
src(18,'The Twelfth Lok Sabha: a historic beginning','Journal of Parliamentary Information','https://eparlib.sansad.in/bitstream/123456789/763122/1/jpi_June_1998.pdf','1998-06','Parliamentary record','Opening article; Council of Ministers','A42-member Council of Ministers was sworn in19 March1998; Advani allocated Home.','Indexed official passage located; original retrieval timed out twice. Exact appointment date remains provisional until full passage access.',status='Indexed passage only')
src(19,'Advani appointed Deputy Prime Minister','Times of India','https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/advani-appointed-deputy-prime-minister/articleshow/14487268.cms','2002-06-29','Journalism','Opening announcement','Presidential notification appointed Home Minister Advani Deputy PM on29 June2002; he retained Home.','Contemporary reporting of notification; canonical appointment notification not collected.')
src(20,'India: domestic politics in2005','Mayumi Murayama; IDE-JETRO, Asian Development Experience/Yearbook','https://www.ide.go.jp/library/English/Publish/Books/Eng_Books/Yearbook/pdf/2006_17.pdf','2006','Academic','PDF pp.8–10; printed467–469','Explains tension between RSS ideological demands and BJP coalition needs. Advani’s Jinnah remarks in Pakistan provoked criticism;7 June resignation was withdrawn. He announced departure in September and resigned formally31 December2005; Rajnath Singh succeeded him.','Contemporary scholarly assessment. Motives are the author’s interpretation; quotations about Jinnah establish what Advani praised.')
src(21,'Jaswant Singh: Walk the Talk interview','Jaswant Singh interviewed by Shekhar Gupta, Indian Express/NDTV','https://indianexpress.com/article/news-archive/web/i-told-advaniji-not-to-associate-himself-with-the-sting-operation-he-kept-quiet-and-i-couldnt-press-beyond-a-point/','2009-08-24','Primary statement','Gujarat discussion lines224–232; Kandahar779–833','Singh recalled Advani warning of party turmoil if action were taken against Modi in2002. On Kandahar, Singh said Advani knew he would travel and that Cabinet/CCS had discussed it, disputing Advani’s recollection.','Retrospective participant account following expulsion from BJP. Supports attributed recollections, not definitive reconstruction of closed Cabinet discussions.',origin='JASWANT-INTERVIEW-2009')
